        "username": "FrivYeti",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-03-17T03:56:22.395Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I’m going to give a fourth interpretation!</p>\n<p>My read was that the damage you dealt was equal to the final result on the effect die (number rolled plus any bonus or penalty), so if you had armor or someone was Defending you, but you still took damage, you reflected the pre-defense amount you would have taken.</p>",
